  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Norarecoline and MOVP-3 through a series of target interactions. Norarecoline is identified as a target of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one and Botryorhodine C. All of these compounds are ultimately linked to MOVP-3. This indicates that Norarecoline may exert its effects through a common intermediary, Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is involved in the metabolism or activity of various compounds, including those that target MOVP-3. The consistent presence of this intermediary in the evidence chain supports a plausible mechanism by which Norarecoline could interact with MOVP-3, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be determined. The evidence is robust and consistent across different pathways, suggesting a well-defined biological relationship."
